WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.893
(steady music)

00:00:10.920 --> 00:00:11.753
- All right.

00:00:12.750 --> 00:00:16.470
Welcome to the Smartphone Awards 2022.

00:00:16.470 --> 00:00:17.460
It's one of my favorite videos.

00:00:17.460 --> 00:00:18.540
Y'all knew it was coming.

00:00:18.540 --> 00:00:19.440
It's a bit of a tradition

00:00:19.440 --> 00:00:21.900
around here to revisit the smartphones

00:00:21.900 --> 00:00:25.260
that came out during
the calendar year 2022.

00:00:25.260 --> 00:00:29.730
And then I like to recognize
and reward some of the best

00:00:29.730 --> 00:00:31.620
and some of the worst that came out

00:00:31.620 --> 00:00:33.150
and some of the interesting
stuff that happened

00:00:33.150 --> 00:00:33.983
during this calendar year.

00:00:33.983 --> 00:00:35.880
There's a lot, usually we forget
about a lot of this stuff,

00:00:35.880 --> 00:00:38.100
but this is one of my
favorite videos to make.

00:00:38.100 --> 00:00:40.860
We even have, of course, no spoilers,

00:00:40.860 --> 00:00:43.980
but we've got some trophies
for the winners as well.

00:00:43.980 --> 00:00:44.813
They're super nice.

00:00:44.813 --> 00:00:48.000
So, from flagships to
midranges to budget phones

00:00:48.000 --> 00:00:52.140
to specialty phones to folding
phones, I got to use 'em all.

00:00:52.140 --> 00:00:55.140
I got, I have my own opinions
about them, and you know,

00:00:55.140 --> 00:00:56.610
some of you may agree
with some of these awards.

00:00:56.610 --> 00:00:57.630
Some of you may disagree,

00:00:57.630 --> 00:01:00.630
but one thing is for sure
is they're my awards.

00:01:00.630 --> 00:01:03.150
So without any further ado,
let's start giving 'em out.

00:01:03.150 --> 00:01:06.270
So, the first category is best big phone.

00:01:06.270 --> 00:01:07.740
Now, I mean, look at this table.

00:01:07.740 --> 00:01:10.200
Obviously, phones have gotten
bigger and bigger over time,

00:01:10.200 --> 00:01:11.910
to the point where pretty
much every phone is big.

00:01:11.910 --> 00:01:14.130
But I still like to reward a phone

00:01:14.130 --> 00:01:16.770
that had a great use of that space

00:01:16.770 --> 00:01:18.300
because you still want a big screen

00:01:18.300 --> 00:01:21.270
but also a big battery,
maybe big speakers,

00:01:21.270 --> 00:01:23.220
some nice cameras, and the whole thing,

00:01:23.220 --> 00:01:26.250
just being a good use
of all that extra space.

00:01:26.250 --> 00:01:28.140
And so, my winner for the best big phone

00:01:28.140 --> 00:01:29.280
of the year actually came out

00:01:29.280 --> 00:01:30.840
right near the beginning of it.

00:01:30.840 --> 00:01:34.649
And that is Samsung's Galaxy S22 Ultra.

00:01:34.649 --> 00:01:37.110
(gentle music)
So hardware-wise, I feel

00:01:37.110 --> 00:01:39.150
like this one just pretty
much did it all here.

00:01:39.150 --> 00:01:40.950
It's got the big 6.8 inch display,

00:01:40.950 --> 00:01:42.870
one of the absolute best in the business.

00:01:42.870 --> 00:01:44.610
It added a stylus

00:01:44.610 --> 00:01:47.220
but still included a 5,000
milliamp hour battery

00:01:47.220 --> 00:01:49.050
which is the same as the year before.

00:01:49.050 --> 00:01:51.090
Multiple great cameras on the back,

00:01:51.090 --> 00:01:54.570
a pair of great telephotos,
good speakers, good software,

00:01:54.570 --> 00:01:56.880
really no hardware flaws to speak of,

00:01:56.880 --> 00:01:58.620
to the point where maybe you'd
say it was kind of boring

00:01:58.620 --> 00:01:59.940
which I think is actually a good thing.

00:01:59.940 --> 00:02:01.590
If you're looking to spend
this much on a phone,

00:02:01.590 --> 00:02:04.560
you don't want anything
to be too weird about it.

00:02:04.560 --> 00:02:07.260
And so, yeah, this one's the category

00:02:07.260 --> 00:02:10.680
in a way that I think the
Notes usually did in the past.

00:02:10.680 --> 00:02:12.780
So, it's sort of a return of the Note.

00:02:12.780 --> 00:02:14.580
But I do also give some runner-ups

00:02:14.580 --> 00:02:16.620
and honorable mentions in
some of these categories too.

00:02:16.620 --> 00:02:18.930
And that's what I'm gonna
do in best big phone,

00:02:18.930 --> 00:02:23.910
which means the runner-up
is the ASUS ROG Phone 6.

00:02:23.910 --> 00:02:26.130
Really similar actually in a lot of ways

00:02:26.130 --> 00:02:28.890
to Samsung's flagships, just
missing a couple little things.

00:02:28.890 --> 00:02:30.930
It's a little more specialized,
no wireless charging,

00:02:30.930 --> 00:02:32.070
but it's got a screen on the back

00:02:32.070 --> 00:02:33.810
and it's much more gaming centric.

00:02:33.810 --> 00:02:35.250
But I got shout it out

00:02:35.250 --> 00:02:39.210
for the incredible, massive
stereo front facing speakers

00:02:39.210 --> 00:02:41.220
and also the headphone jack.

00:02:41.220 --> 00:02:43.740
Big phone, it should have
room for a headphones jack.

00:02:43.740 --> 00:02:44.670
And then also a little shout out,

00:02:44.670 --> 00:02:48.030
a little honorable mention
to the Xiaomi Mix Fold 2.

00:02:48.030 --> 00:02:50.490
This, it didn't have an IP
rating, it wasn't quite,

00:02:50.490 --> 00:02:52.380
you know, available
for everyone worldwide.

00:02:52.380 --> 00:02:53.970
But this is one of those folding phones

00:02:53.970 --> 00:02:58.470
where it folded just to
about the same thickness

00:02:58.470 --> 00:02:59.790
as a normal phone,

00:02:59.790 --> 00:03:02.070
which is sort of like one of
those breakthrough moments

00:03:02.070 --> 00:03:03.480
in folding phones, I think.

00:03:03.480 --> 00:03:05.340
And now we can start to feel like they're

00:03:05.340 --> 00:03:07.170
on their way towards being usable.

00:03:07.170 --> 00:03:09.510
Big phone, smaller package.
(phone clicking)

00:03:09.510 --> 00:03:10.740
All right, next category,

00:03:10.740 --> 00:03:12.420
best small phone.

00:03:12.420 --> 00:03:14.490
So now, we're on the other
end of the spectrum, right?

00:03:14.490 --> 00:03:15.930
There are not a lot of small phones

00:03:15.930 --> 00:03:17.700
and this is a rare category.

00:03:17.700 --> 00:03:20.100
And I'll be honest, this one wasn't close.

00:03:20.100 --> 00:03:21.900
So, last year's winner,
as you might recall,

00:03:21.900 --> 00:03:23.820
was the iPhone Mini.

00:03:23.820 --> 00:03:25.170
They killed that this year,

00:03:25.170 --> 00:03:26.940
so that wasn't even gonna qualify.

00:03:26.940 --> 00:03:30.120
So, what would be the best
small phone of the year?

00:03:30.120 --> 00:03:31.800
It's the best small phone I've ever seen.

00:03:31.800 --> 00:03:35.610
And that is ASUS Zenfone 9.

00:03:35.610 --> 00:03:38.430
This phone is so nice
(gentle music)

00:03:38.430 --> 00:03:40.530
and they made a lot of great decisions

00:03:40.530 --> 00:03:41.370
across the board here.

00:03:41.370 --> 00:03:44.460
So, small, it's relative,
but it's a 5.9 inch display,

00:03:44.460 --> 00:03:46.860
relatively compact, flagship specs,

00:03:46.860 --> 00:03:49.380
Snapdragon 8+ Gen 1, a 1080p,

00:03:49.380 --> 00:03:52.350
higher refresh rate, OLED, great software,

00:03:52.350 --> 00:03:55.830
tons of ram, really fast, and
a surprisingly great camera.

00:03:55.830 --> 00:03:58.590
And if this phone this small
can have a headphone jack,

00:03:58.590 --> 00:04:00.510
then what's everybody else's excuse?

00:04:00.510 --> 00:04:01.680
Right?

00:04:01.680 --> 00:04:03.180
There are a lot of great
things I liked about it.

00:04:03.180 --> 00:04:05.430
It did have a couple weird flaws,

00:04:05.430 --> 00:04:07.500
like this weird soft touchback

00:04:07.500 --> 00:04:08.670
that ended up discoloring a lot.

00:04:08.670 --> 00:04:09.900
I talked about that in the main review.

00:04:09.900 --> 00:04:12.870
But like, man, I was very surprised

00:04:12.870 --> 00:04:14.550
by the battery life on this phone.

00:04:14.550 --> 00:04:16.380
There's not a lot of things
I get genuinely surprised

00:04:16.380 --> 00:04:17.460
about in the smartphone world now,

00:04:17.460 --> 00:04:20.460
but a phone in this small having
such a great battery life,

00:04:20.460 --> 00:04:23.847
this is easily, easy, best
smartphone in this size.

00:04:23.847 --> 00:04:25.410
But I will give a little
honorable mention,

00:04:25.410 --> 00:04:27.090
a little runner up though,

00:04:27.090 --> 00:04:28.200
because there was a certain phone

00:04:28.200 --> 00:04:30.600
that came out right at
the very end of the year.

00:04:30.600 --> 00:04:32.850
You guys might have wondered
why this video was so late.

00:04:32.850 --> 00:04:34.800
I'll give partial credit to this one.

00:04:34.800 --> 00:04:39.480
Oppo Find N2, this is that
little passport sized phone.

00:04:39.480 --> 00:04:42.720
It's got these flat edges and
it's still a folding phone

00:04:42.720 --> 00:04:45.390
which has got a pretty
solid display on the inside.

00:04:45.390 --> 00:04:46.770
I haven't done a full review about it yet

00:04:46.770 --> 00:04:48.413
but it feels like
(phone clicking)

00:04:48.413 --> 00:04:50.370
this is a bit of a preview

00:04:50.370 --> 00:04:54.240
to what a folding Pixel might look like

00:04:54.240 --> 00:04:55.140
which is really interesting.

00:04:55.140 --> 00:04:56.850
But all right, let's
get to the next category

00:04:56.850 --> 00:05:01.850
which is best camera, or should
I say, best camera system

00:05:02.370 --> 00:05:03.203
across the board?

00:05:03.203 --> 00:05:04.680
Because there is a lot to a good camera

00:05:04.680 --> 00:05:07.860
from photo quality to video quality

00:05:07.860 --> 00:05:11.520
but also speed of capture
and auto-focus reliability

00:05:11.520 --> 00:05:14.400
and ease of use and file formats
and all this other stuff.

00:05:14.400 --> 00:05:15.750
So, we did something really
interesting this year.

00:05:15.750 --> 00:05:17.790
We did a blind smartphone camera test

00:05:17.790 --> 00:05:20.190
in the form of a website that we built

00:05:20.190 --> 00:05:22.050
where we gave everyone the ability to vote

00:05:22.050 --> 00:05:25.140
on whatever photos they like
in three different categories.

00:05:25.140 --> 00:05:27.180
And we had 16 different phones

00:05:27.180 --> 00:05:29.670
from the year all competing
against each other.

00:05:29.670 --> 00:05:31.470
And the overall winner

00:05:31.470 --> 00:05:36.470
across all three categories
was the Pixel 6A, incredibly.

00:05:36.630 --> 00:05:39.360
And actually, runner up
to it was the Pixel 7.

00:05:39.360 --> 00:05:42.780
So, these are clearly some
really good photo quality phones

00:05:42.780 --> 00:05:45.780
but I'm not giving them the
trophy for best camera system.

00:05:45.780 --> 00:05:48.710
I'm also not giving it
to the vivo X80 Pro+

00:05:48.710 --> 00:05:52.680
or X90 Pro+, which were low light kings.

00:05:52.680 --> 00:05:54.090
They had a really great combination

00:05:54.090 --> 00:05:57.090
of software and a really
impressive sensor.

00:05:57.090 --> 00:05:59.490
The hardware stack is great, but no,

00:05:59.490 --> 00:06:03.990
my winner for best overall camera system

00:06:03.990 --> 00:06:08.563
in 2022 is going to the iPhone 14 Pros.

00:06:08.563 --> 00:06:09.750
(gentle music)

00:06:09.750 --> 00:06:12.510
So, this has now become the
longest defending champion

00:06:12.510 --> 00:06:14.220
of a single category ever.

00:06:14.220 --> 00:06:15.060
This is the fourth year

00:06:15.060 --> 00:06:18.330
in a row the iPhone has taken
down the camera category,

00:06:18.330 --> 00:06:20.550
because again, it's
great across the board.

00:06:20.550 --> 00:06:23.190
So, image quality as we
know is solid, right?

00:06:23.190 --> 00:06:24.023
We knew that.

00:06:24.023 --> 00:06:25.590
But the time to open the camera

00:06:25.590 --> 00:06:28.080
to actually snap a photo
is extremely quick.

00:06:28.080 --> 00:06:29.520
The auto focus is fast.

00:06:29.520 --> 00:06:31.260
I'd say, you could fairly
give the Pro iPhones

00:06:31.260 --> 00:06:33.840
like an A minus to a B plus for photos.

00:06:33.840 --> 00:06:35.460
But then in the video department,

00:06:35.460 --> 00:06:37.080
it's a whole different dimension

00:06:37.080 --> 00:06:38.820
and it's not really even close.

00:06:38.820 --> 00:06:41.400
I've been running the
auto-focus YouTube channel now

00:06:41.400 --> 00:06:44.280
for a couple months, doing
a lot of videos on cars,

00:06:44.280 --> 00:06:46.260
shot entirely on smartphones.

00:06:46.260 --> 00:06:47.490
And you can tell the difference

00:06:47.490 --> 00:06:50.280
when I shot a video on the iPhone's camera

00:06:50.280 --> 00:06:52.170
versus the other smartphone cameras.

00:06:52.170 --> 00:06:53.640
It's how good it looks.

00:06:53.640 --> 00:06:54.870
It's the audio quality.

00:06:54.870 --> 00:06:56.520
It's the consistency of color.

00:06:56.520 --> 00:06:58.770
It's the pro res, the sharpness.

00:06:58.770 --> 00:07:00.447
I much prefer shooting videos on iPhones

00:07:00.447 --> 00:07:01.980
and I think I'm not alone there.

00:07:01.980 --> 00:07:03.840
And I'll say, it still takes a long time

00:07:03.840 --> 00:07:05.280
to get the files off of the iPhone

00:07:05.280 --> 00:07:06.870
and I hope they fix that.

00:07:06.870 --> 00:07:08.760
But it's the winner
for best camera system.

00:07:08.760 --> 00:07:10.350
Okay, so next up, let's do the battery.

00:07:10.350 --> 00:07:12.750
This is the best battery overall.

00:07:12.750 --> 00:07:13.583
I think this is one

00:07:13.583 --> 00:07:16.410
of the more objective categories probably,

00:07:16.410 --> 00:07:19.050
but it's including a
little more, obviously,

00:07:19.050 --> 00:07:20.550
than just the battery size.

00:07:20.550 --> 00:07:22.980
I wanna include just
the battery experience,

00:07:22.980 --> 00:07:26.340
how long it takes to charge,
how long it lasts on a charge,

00:07:26.340 --> 00:07:29.220
battery flexibility of
features and things like that,

00:07:29.220 --> 00:07:30.660
how long the battery health does.

00:07:30.660 --> 00:07:31.680
And so, my winner

00:07:31.680 --> 00:07:36.680
for best battery in a 2022
phone, it is a defending champ.

00:07:37.170 --> 00:07:40.980
It is the ASUS ROG Phone 6.
(gentle music)

00:07:40.980 --> 00:07:43.860
This one has not a 4,000, not a 5,000,

00:07:43.860 --> 00:07:46.860
but a 6,000 milliamp hour battery.

00:07:46.860 --> 00:07:48.660
It's got 65 watt fast charging,

00:07:48.660 --> 00:07:50.790
so you can go from zero
to full in under an hour.

00:07:50.790 --> 00:07:51.623
And on top of that,

00:07:51.623 --> 00:07:54.480
there is a bevy of battery
management features.

00:07:54.480 --> 00:07:56.880
So obviously, you can
turn the 165 hertz display

00:07:56.880 --> 00:07:58.260
down all the way to 60 hertz

00:07:58.260 --> 00:08:00.330
if you want to and get a ton of battery.

00:08:00.330 --> 00:08:02.520
But then there's also like
charge limit features,

00:08:02.520 --> 00:08:04.500
pass through charging, things like that.

00:08:04.500 --> 00:08:06.480
This phone is a king

00:08:06.480 --> 00:08:07.920
as far as battery life experience

00:08:07.920 --> 00:08:08.880
and it actually charges fast.

00:08:08.880 --> 00:08:10.080
Probably the only knock against it is

00:08:10.080 --> 00:08:11.580
that it doesn't have wireless charging,

00:08:11.580 --> 00:08:14.700
which most other phones in
its price range do have.

00:08:14.700 --> 00:08:17.760
But as far as just worry-free
battery, that's the winner.

00:08:17.760 --> 00:08:19.530
And I will give a runner up

00:08:19.530 --> 00:08:23.400
in this category to the iPhone 14 Plus.

00:08:23.400 --> 00:08:24.750
So, a lot of us kind of saw this coming

00:08:24.750 --> 00:08:26.520
when Apple killed the Mini iPhone

00:08:26.520 --> 00:08:29.610
in favor of a plus-sized iPhone

00:08:29.610 --> 00:08:32.340
that doesn't have the
promotion OLED display.

00:08:32.340 --> 00:08:35.880
So, this is a big, simple 60 hertz display

00:08:35.880 --> 00:08:38.940
that is just powered by a
massive battery in the iPhone,

00:08:38.940 --> 00:08:40.500
massive four in iPhone.

00:08:40.500 --> 00:08:42.120
And so, with wireless charging

00:08:42.120 --> 00:08:43.740
and with all the other
things that Apple does

00:08:43.740 --> 00:08:46.290
to prevent batteries from having problems,

00:08:46.290 --> 00:08:48.720
I'd say that's a pretty
great battery experience.

00:08:48.720 --> 00:08:51.270
And I'll also give a quick
shout out, an honorable mention,

00:08:51.270 --> 00:08:54.210
because the ASUS Zenfone 9, I gotta,

00:08:54.210 --> 00:08:55.620
I keep coming back to this,

00:08:55.620 --> 00:08:57.600
the way it surprised me with battery life.

00:08:57.600 --> 00:09:00.270
This is a 4,300 milliamp
battery in this phone.

00:09:00.270 --> 00:09:02.220
It also doesn't have wireless charging.

00:09:02.220 --> 00:09:04.020
The charging speed is decent,

00:09:04.020 --> 00:09:05.880
but I was genuinely shocked

00:09:05.880 --> 00:09:08.160
by how well this phone held up on battery.

00:09:08.160 --> 00:09:10.290
It's, who would've
thought that a phone small

00:09:10.290 --> 00:09:12.930
like this would've one
of the best batteries

00:09:12.930 --> 00:09:15.360
of any phone that came out
during the calendar year?

00:09:15.360 --> 00:09:18.813
But anyway, okay, next
up is the design award.

00:09:19.680 --> 00:09:21.750
I feel like this is the
hardest one every year

00:09:21.750 --> 00:09:22.890
to think of or to give out,

00:09:22.890 --> 00:09:25.110
just because it is the
most subjective now.

00:09:25.110 --> 00:09:27.300
This is, it's actually
changed over the years.

00:09:27.300 --> 00:09:30.870
It used to be, I think I
called it best build quality

00:09:30.870 --> 00:09:32.520
or just best overall build

00:09:32.520 --> 00:09:34.320
or materials or industrial design.

00:09:34.320 --> 00:09:36.690
But it's eventually
just evolved into like,

00:09:36.690 --> 00:09:38.460
who can step outside of the box

00:09:38.460 --> 00:09:41.100
and do things a little
different design-wise?

00:09:41.100 --> 00:09:43.110
'Cause that honestly
does not happen very much

00:09:43.110 --> 00:09:44.070
in smartphones these days.

00:09:44.070 --> 00:09:45.420
And sometimes, it kind
of feels like a process

00:09:45.420 --> 00:09:46.320
of elimination, like, oh,

00:09:46.320 --> 00:09:49.980
I can't give this to a phone
that played it too safe, right?

00:09:49.980 --> 00:09:52.560
Lots of phones look basically
the same as last year.

00:09:52.560 --> 00:09:54.180
I definitely can't give it to a phone

00:09:54.180 --> 00:09:56.070
that made like an obvious regression

00:09:56.070 --> 00:09:58.470
from the year before or
has like a glaring issue

00:09:58.470 --> 00:10:00.210
with build or materials

00:10:00.210 --> 00:10:02.700
or failed, jerry rig,
everything's test or something.

00:10:02.700 --> 00:10:04.483
I can't give it to an
iPhone either, can I?

00:10:04.483 --> 00:10:06.540
I mean, they still have the biggest notch,

00:10:06.540 --> 00:10:09.150
but, oh there's the
Dynamic Island though too.

00:10:09.150 --> 00:10:11.490
Maybe, no.

00:10:11.490 --> 00:10:15.130
The design award for 2022 is gonna go

00:10:16.890 --> 00:10:18.780
to the Nothing phone.

00:10:18.780 --> 00:10:20.493
The Nothing Phone won.

00:10:22.260 --> 00:10:24.510
Get it?
(gentle music)

00:10:24.510 --> 00:10:27.120
The design I think is
literally the best thing

00:10:27.120 --> 00:10:29.190
about this phone, maybe second best.

00:10:29.190 --> 00:10:31.590
So, it's got this sort of transparent look

00:10:31.590 --> 00:10:33.360
which is definitely trying something new.

00:10:33.360 --> 00:10:36.390
And then the glyph interface
with these lights on the back,

00:10:36.390 --> 00:10:38.100
they light up for notifications.

00:10:38.100 --> 00:10:39.360
They can also light up

00:10:39.360 --> 00:10:41.940
as a fill flash for video if you want.

00:10:41.940 --> 00:10:44.460
It also has a wireless
charging indicator on the back.

00:10:44.460 --> 00:10:45.990
It definitely skirts the line

00:10:45.990 --> 00:10:47.940
right between gimmick and feature.

00:10:47.940 --> 00:10:49.380
Like, a lot of people will get this phone

00:10:49.380 --> 00:10:51.720
and have fun with it for a week
and then never use it again.

00:10:51.720 --> 00:10:53.070
But I find it really neat.

00:10:53.070 --> 00:10:53.903
I think it's cool

00:10:53.903 --> 00:10:55.680
that you can see how much
battery is as you're charging.

00:10:55.680 --> 00:10:57.180
I don't know, little things like that.

00:10:57.180 --> 00:10:59.130
You don't see a lot of
phones trying new stuff.

00:10:59.130 --> 00:11:01.560
The rest of the phone happens
to be pretty good too.

00:11:01.560 --> 00:11:04.050
So, I have no problem
giving the Nothing Phone

00:11:04.050 --> 00:11:05.610
the design award for 2022.

00:11:05.610 --> 00:11:07.500
And then I do also want to
give an honorable mention

00:11:07.500 --> 00:11:11.760
in design to that Xiaomi Mix Fold 2.

00:11:11.760 --> 00:11:13.200
There were a number of folding phones

00:11:13.200 --> 00:11:15.210
that came out during this year,

00:11:15.210 --> 00:11:16.560
but as I mentioned earlier,

00:11:16.560 --> 00:11:20.610
this is the first one that
sort of passed that barrier

00:11:20.610 --> 00:11:24.690
of actually being the same
thickness as a normal phone.

00:11:24.690 --> 00:11:25.523
I mean, look at,

00:11:25.523 --> 00:11:27.055
this is another phone that
came out during this year.

00:11:27.055 --> 00:11:29.940
It's very close in overall thickness.

00:11:29.940 --> 00:11:31.290
So, a lot of phones you pick up,

00:11:31.290 --> 00:11:32.640
like this is Samsung's folding, you,

00:11:32.640 --> 00:11:34.680
it just feel, it's thicker
than a normal phone.

00:11:34.680 --> 00:11:36.150
And you'd think about that all the time

00:11:36.150 --> 00:11:36.983
when you're using it.

00:11:36.983 --> 00:11:39.000
So, I wanted to reward this
one for actually getting

00:11:39.000 --> 00:11:40.710
to that point where now,

00:11:40.710 --> 00:11:43.260
there's other things to fix
still about folding phones,

00:11:43.260 --> 00:11:46.290
but this feels very usable and pocketable

00:11:46.290 --> 00:11:48.030
and gives you the benefits of unfolding

00:11:48.030 --> 00:11:48.901
to a huge screen.

00:11:48.901 --> 00:11:49.980
(phone clicking)
Shout out to Xiaomi.

00:11:49.980 --> 00:11:51.840
All right, let's give out a value award.

00:11:51.840 --> 00:11:52.673
I like this one.

00:11:52.673 --> 00:11:53.580
This is,

00:11:53.580 --> 00:11:56.190
this was actually pretty
close as well this year too.

00:11:56.190 --> 00:11:58.590
Notice it's one of the
more controversial awards.

00:11:58.590 --> 00:12:01.560
It used to be best budget phone

00:12:01.560 --> 00:12:04.350
but budget means something
different for everyone.

00:12:04.350 --> 00:12:07.170
So, I'm just calling this
like best bang for the buck.

00:12:07.170 --> 00:12:09.810
You can kind of picture
the pyramid of phones,

00:12:09.810 --> 00:12:11.220
and when you see a good one,

00:12:11.220 --> 00:12:12.330
you know what I'm talking about.

00:12:12.330 --> 00:12:13.950
When you see a phone
that has a great price,

00:12:13.950 --> 00:12:16.050
I'm going by launch price, MSRP.

00:12:16.050 --> 00:12:19.860
So, the winner, my, I'm giving
my winning by a little bit,

00:12:19.860 --> 00:12:23.790
best value award to the Pixel 7.

00:12:23.790 --> 00:12:27.180
This phone came out at 599
(gentle music)

00:12:27.180 --> 00:12:29.940
and it's one of the best
599 phones I have ever seen.

00:12:29.940 --> 00:12:30.773
I mean it's pretty clear.

00:12:30.773 --> 00:12:33.180
It's the whole Google flagship experience.

00:12:33.180 --> 00:12:35.040
It's also got the tensor chip flagship,

00:12:35.040 --> 00:12:36.510
same as the more expensive one.

00:12:36.510 --> 00:12:38.490
It's also got the same main sensor,

00:12:38.490 --> 00:12:41.250
the same flagship camera
as the more expensive one.

00:12:41.250 --> 00:12:44.130
It has a great 90 hertz OLED flat display.

00:12:44.130 --> 00:12:46.830
It's so good that it made
the 7 Pro kind of feel

00:12:46.830 --> 00:12:47.663
like not that good of a deal

00:12:47.663 --> 00:12:51.030
'cause 599, there is not
a lot that you can get

00:12:51.030 --> 00:12:53.220
for this price that does this well.

00:12:53.220 --> 00:12:55.140
In fact, I'd argue nothing.

00:12:55.140 --> 00:12:56.760
So, this is one of my favorite phones

00:12:56.760 --> 00:12:58.230
that came out this year,

00:12:58.230 --> 00:13:00.990
but it just barely beats out another one

00:13:00.990 --> 00:13:03.060
of my favorite phones
that came out this year

00:13:03.060 --> 00:13:08.060
which is ASUS Zenfone
9, really unique combo

00:13:08.160 --> 00:13:10.800
for this one which launched at 699.

00:13:10.800 --> 00:13:13.830
It also now has the Snapdragon 8+ Gen 1.

00:13:13.830 --> 00:13:16.620
It's got a ton of ram, 120 Hertz display,

00:13:16.620 --> 00:13:17.730
a flat OLED again,

00:13:17.730 --> 00:13:20.130
but also like the fingerprint
reader on the side,

00:13:20.130 --> 00:13:22.350
a headphone jack and
incredible battery life.

00:13:22.350 --> 00:13:23.910
I mean these two phones
could go back and forth

00:13:23.910 --> 00:13:24.743
head to head.

00:13:24.743 --> 00:13:26.400
I could easily be swayed here.

00:13:26.400 --> 00:13:28.800
But those two were awesome to see.

00:13:28.800 --> 00:13:30.840
That's probably the best
699 phone I've ever seen.

00:13:30.840 --> 00:13:33.990
And among the myriad of other
really good sub $400 phones

00:13:33.990 --> 00:13:35.700
that came out, I want to
give an honorable mention

00:13:35.700 --> 00:13:38.220
to the Realme 10 Pro+.

00:13:38.220 --> 00:13:40.440
This had a big 6.7 inch display.

00:13:40.440 --> 00:13:41.760
You can see the cameras on the back,

00:13:41.760 --> 00:13:43.500
5,000 milliamp hour battery.

00:13:43.500 --> 00:13:45.780
But this camera performed
surprisingly well

00:13:45.780 --> 00:13:46.860
to a lot of people.

00:13:46.860 --> 00:13:48.570
It ended up beating thousand dollar phones

00:13:48.570 --> 00:13:50.910
and it was second place
in votes per dollar

00:13:50.910 --> 00:13:52.830
in our blind smartphone camera test.

00:13:52.830 --> 00:13:56.160
Really good overall package
for about 350 bucks.

00:13:56.160 --> 00:13:57.270
I like the way this launched

00:13:57.270 --> 00:14:00.660
and I think if you can get
over the way it shines,

00:14:00.660 --> 00:14:01.500
it's a really good one.

00:14:01.500 --> 00:14:03.033
All right, bust of the year.

00:14:04.020 --> 00:14:05.700
You know, we give it out every year.

00:14:05.700 --> 00:14:07.560
You don't like giving it out,

00:14:07.560 --> 00:14:09.693
but it's the one you hate to have to give.

00:14:10.650 --> 00:14:11.670
You know, there's a lot of phones

00:14:11.670 --> 00:14:14.280
that played it really
safe, which is interesting.

00:14:14.280 --> 00:14:17.910
And you could argue for
a lot of boring phones

00:14:17.910 --> 00:14:20.910
to just have been too
boring, bust of the year,

00:14:20.910 --> 00:14:23.970
I wish they did something
more exciting or interesting

00:14:23.970 --> 00:14:25.350
but I don't know.

00:14:25.350 --> 00:14:27.480
A lot of phones these
days are very similar

00:14:27.480 --> 00:14:29.430
to their previous years and
I won't penalize 'em for that

00:14:29.430 --> 00:14:30.960
if the previous phone is good.

00:14:30.960 --> 00:14:33.930
I really only had one
pick for bust of the year

00:14:33.930 --> 00:14:37.800
and that's the OnePlus 10T,
(gentle music)

00:14:37.800 --> 00:14:40.770
not a whole ton to say here.

00:14:40.770 --> 00:14:44.490
It wins this award for
having a pretty big delta

00:14:44.490 --> 00:14:49.490
between expectations and
possibilities versus actual result.

00:14:49.800 --> 00:14:52.080
Not all of that is OnePlus's fault,

00:14:52.080 --> 00:14:55.170
but I mean they've been on
this slight downward trend

00:14:55.170 --> 00:14:59.790
of value and reputation
and software experience

00:14:59.790 --> 00:15:02.400
and cameras and a whole bunch
of other things like that.

00:15:02.400 --> 00:15:03.600
There's just not a whole lot to like,

00:15:03.600 --> 00:15:05.940
and it also just feels
like the identity has sort

00:15:05.940 --> 00:15:08.340
of been eroded very quickly over time.

00:15:08.340 --> 00:15:10.620
We just had the Hasselblad thing added

00:15:10.620 --> 00:15:12.960
to the previous OnePlus flagship phone

00:15:12.960 --> 00:15:14.790
and then the 10T comes out

00:15:14.790 --> 00:15:16.410
and they don't even bother with it.

00:15:16.410 --> 00:15:18.120
I don't know if they're
saving it for the pro phones,

00:15:18.120 --> 00:15:19.440
but it's like, what do you, what is this?

00:15:19.440 --> 00:15:22.170
What do you even say about
OnePlus phones anymore?

00:15:22.170 --> 00:15:24.870
There's no, you can't even
describe a OnePlus phone

00:15:24.870 --> 00:15:27.000
without feeling really generic.

00:15:27.000 --> 00:15:30.330
So anyway, yeah, congrats on
your award, bust of the year.

00:15:30.330 --> 00:15:33.180
So that brings us to the MVP,

00:15:33.180 --> 00:15:34.770
the most valuable phone?

00:15:34.770 --> 00:15:36.690
Nah, it's not the value award, it's the,

00:15:36.690 --> 00:15:37.740
it's my favorites list.

00:15:37.740 --> 00:15:39.060
That's kind of what this has turned into.

00:15:39.060 --> 00:15:42.630
Like, the best overall phone combined

00:15:42.630 --> 00:15:44.880
with the best overall experience,

00:15:44.880 --> 00:15:46.950
the best impact on the industry.

00:15:46.950 --> 00:15:48.570
There's a bunch of different things

00:15:48.570 --> 00:15:51.450
that can float you to the
top of my favorites list

00:15:51.450 --> 00:15:52.800
from the smartphones
that came out this year.

00:15:52.800 --> 00:15:53.910
And there are a lot of really good ones.

00:15:53.910 --> 00:15:55.650
You've just heard about great cameras,

00:15:55.650 --> 00:15:57.600
great big phones, great battery lives,

00:15:57.600 --> 00:16:00.000
great value, some surprises.

00:16:00.000 --> 00:16:05.000
This was a really close
one for me, really tough.

00:16:05.130 --> 00:16:07.710
Again, I could be swayed.

00:16:07.710 --> 00:16:09.300
I don't even wanna say that about the MVP,

00:16:09.300 --> 00:16:10.500
but I really think it's that close.

00:16:10.500 --> 00:16:12.210
I have two MVPs, okay?

00:16:12.210 --> 00:16:16.140
But I'm giving my top dog,
my number one MVP award

00:16:16.140 --> 00:16:19.271
for 2022 to the Pixel 7.

00:16:19.271 --> 00:16:20.520
(gentle music)
This phone,

00:16:20.520 --> 00:16:21.930
it deserves it for sure.

00:16:21.930 --> 00:16:24.930
Like you heard about in its previous win,

00:16:24.930 --> 00:16:26.760
great value, okay?

00:16:26.760 --> 00:16:29.550
Incredible cameras, great display,

00:16:29.550 --> 00:16:33.270
flagship software experience,
really good battery life,

00:16:33.270 --> 00:16:34.890
not a whole lot missing.

00:16:34.890 --> 00:16:35.970
And that's kind of what you get

00:16:35.970 --> 00:16:37.860
with a phone like this,
which is like, all right,

00:16:37.860 --> 00:16:41.100
the 7 Pro came out for 300 more dollars.

00:16:41.100 --> 00:16:41.940
And that's actually a phone

00:16:41.940 --> 00:16:43.470
that I've used a lot to this day.

00:16:43.470 --> 00:16:45.930
But what do you really get more for that?

00:16:45.930 --> 00:16:49.170
The telephoto camera, the
extra 30 hertz on the display,

00:16:49.170 --> 00:16:51.330
like this phone is such a good deal

00:16:51.330 --> 00:16:53.520
that it's hard to recommend the 7 Pro.

00:16:53.520 --> 00:16:55.950
I love recommending the 7.

00:16:55.950 --> 00:16:57.300
It's just an overall excellent phone

00:16:57.300 --> 00:17:00.060
and I'm glad that Google
found their groove

00:17:00.060 --> 00:17:02.370
'cause I actually just forgot,

00:17:02.370 --> 00:17:05.190
I haven't given out the most
improved award yet either.

00:17:05.190 --> 00:17:07.022
And that's also the Pixel 7.

00:17:07.022 --> 00:17:08.640
(gentle music)
Google really found

00:17:08.640 --> 00:17:10.200
their groove with this phone.

00:17:10.200 --> 00:17:11.280
And to be fair, there are a lot

00:17:11.280 --> 00:17:13.050
of people who might criticize the design.

00:17:13.050 --> 00:17:15.300
They don't like, you
know, the visor as much.

00:17:15.300 --> 00:17:16.800
I kind of like the glass visor

00:17:16.800 --> 00:17:19.080
of the 6 a little bit more
to be perfectly honest.

00:17:19.080 --> 00:17:20.370
But I actually like that it's unique.

00:17:20.370 --> 00:17:22.020
If you look at a phone from far away,

00:17:22.020 --> 00:17:24.060
you know exactly what a
Pixel phone looks like.

00:17:24.060 --> 00:17:25.080
From across the street,

00:17:25.080 --> 00:17:26.730
you know what a pixel looks like, right?

00:17:26.730 --> 00:17:28.290
They're doing this advertising thing.

00:17:28.290 --> 00:17:30.180
They're actually getting
into people's hands.

00:17:30.180 --> 00:17:31.500
I just did my assistant battle,

00:17:31.500 --> 00:17:33.900
and like, the assistant
that runs on this phone,

00:17:33.900 --> 00:17:36.030
especially on the Pixel, is excellent.

00:17:36.030 --> 00:17:38.430
The voice recorder app,
all the smart features,

00:17:38.430 --> 00:17:41.190
hold for me, the screen call feature.

00:17:41.190 --> 00:17:43.620
I just, I can't say enough good things.

00:17:43.620 --> 00:17:48.120
Pixel 7, great package,
overall, love this phone.

00:17:48.120 --> 00:17:49.920
So, why am I so torn?

00:17:49.920 --> 00:17:52.650
What is the other phone
that is such a good year

00:17:52.650 --> 00:17:55.563
that I have a hard time
only picking one MVP?

00:17:56.820 --> 00:17:58.320
Well, it's the Zenfone 9, baby.

00:17:58.320 --> 00:18:01.680
This phone, this had a lot
of good things going for it,

00:18:01.680 --> 00:18:03.030
and it was one of my favorite phones,

00:18:03.030 --> 00:18:04.620
one of my biggest surprises of the year.

00:18:04.620 --> 00:18:05.880
Where do I start?

00:18:05.880 --> 00:18:07.410
The design I really liked,

00:18:07.410 --> 00:18:11.070
despite not having the best
wear and tear experience.

00:18:11.070 --> 00:18:12.150
I'm not a big case person,

00:18:12.150 --> 00:18:13.740
so I gotta give it a knock for that.

00:18:13.740 --> 00:18:14.820
No wireless charging.

00:18:14.820 --> 00:18:18.330
But the Snapdragon 8+ Gen
1 had amazing performance.

00:18:18.330 --> 00:18:21.420
This phone's battery life was incredible.

00:18:21.420 --> 00:18:23.850
It didn't charge fast, but
like I was just amazed by that.

00:18:23.850 --> 00:18:25.380
It has a headphone jack.

00:18:25.380 --> 00:18:27.330
It has the fingerprint reader on the side

00:18:27.330 --> 00:18:28.260
which was very fast

00:18:28.260 --> 00:18:31.680
but also had gestures and
surprisingly good cameras.

00:18:31.680 --> 00:18:35.310
I mean, these things ended
up top five, top four,

00:18:35.310 --> 00:18:37.860
maybe top three in our blind
smartphone camera test,

00:18:37.860 --> 00:18:39.630
voted by the masses.

00:18:39.630 --> 00:18:42.210
So, ASUS has had great cameras for years.

00:18:42.210 --> 00:18:45.030
I just really liked this phone.

00:18:45.030 --> 00:18:45.900
It's more expensive.

00:18:45.900 --> 00:18:47.640
It was 699 on launch.

00:18:47.640 --> 00:18:48.690
I think they did this weird thing

00:18:48.690 --> 00:18:50.070
in the US where it launched for more.

00:18:50.070 --> 00:18:52.530
But like, if you can get
your hands on this phone

00:18:52.530 --> 00:18:54.150
and pop a sim card tray in it

00:18:54.150 --> 00:18:56.910
and it actually will work
well with your carrier,

00:18:56.910 --> 00:19:01.910
the Zenfone 9 was a very close
second for my MVP for 2022.

00:19:02.340 --> 00:19:03.173
But then one more,

00:19:03.173 --> 00:19:04.230
I want to give an honorable mention

00:19:04.230 --> 00:19:07.980
to the old boring Galaxy S22 Ultra.

00:19:07.980 --> 00:19:10.890
It's an expensive phone, it
has all the hardware features.

00:19:10.890 --> 00:19:12.120
It didn't really do anything wrong.

00:19:12.120 --> 00:19:13.410
It just happens to have one

00:19:13.410 --> 00:19:15.240
of the biggest batteries
and the best display

00:19:15.240 --> 00:19:16.073
in the business

00:19:16.073 --> 00:19:18.300
and one of the best camera
suites in the business

00:19:18.300 --> 00:19:19.860
and one of the best processors.

00:19:19.860 --> 00:19:22.950
I mean, it's a boring,
really solid overall phone

00:19:22.950 --> 00:19:24.330
and that's why it won best big phone.

00:19:24.330 --> 00:19:25.650
And so, I'll give it
that honorable mention

00:19:25.650 --> 00:19:27.000
because a lot of us wanna see the,

00:19:27.000 --> 00:19:29.040
just the best overall phone
of the year highlighted

00:19:29.040 --> 00:19:32.040
and specs-wise and what
it does for people,

00:19:32.040 --> 00:19:34.110
I think that's a really
good phone to pick,

00:19:34.110 --> 00:19:36.360
of course, right alongside
the ROG phone, I could go on.

00:19:36.360 --> 00:19:38.400
Lots of great phones came out this year,

00:19:38.400 --> 00:19:42.270
but that's been it for the
Smartphone Awards of 2022.

00:19:42.270 --> 00:19:44.220
Feel free to leave all the notes

00:19:44.220 --> 00:19:45.210
in the comment sections below.

00:19:45.210 --> 00:19:46.710
I know all of you guys
will have thoughts on this,

00:19:46.710 --> 00:19:47.670
as we do every year.

00:19:47.670 --> 00:19:48.870
We'll talk about it.

00:19:48.870 --> 00:19:50.880
But of course, if you're
a company seeing this

00:19:50.880 --> 00:19:53.520
and you want your trophy, let me know.

00:19:53.520 --> 00:19:54.600
Hit me up on Twitter or something.

00:19:54.600 --> 00:19:55.860
I'll literally ship it out to you.

00:19:55.860 --> 00:19:57.240
I've done that before.

00:19:57.240 --> 00:19:59.520
Okay, that's been it.

00:19:59.520 --> 00:20:00.394
Thanks for watching.

00:20:00.394 --> 00:20:01.227
♪ Talk to me ♪

00:20:01.227 --> 00:20:02.700
- Alicia Keys said she
liked my jacket one time.

00:20:02.700 --> 00:20:04.008
All right, see you later.

00:20:04.008 --> 00:20:04.841
Peace.

00:20:04.841 --> 00:20:07.424
(steady music)

